  "response": "### Product Decision and Native Test Gate\n\n**Product Decision:**\n- **Lock-Screen Reminder Privacy:** Implement a feature that allows users to opt-in or opt-out of lock-screen reminders. This should be configurable per reminder.\n- **Six-Occurrence Scheduling Horizon:** Allow reminders to be scheduled up to six occurrences in the future. This should be configurable per reminder.\n- **Local Wall-Clock Recurrence and DST Handling:** Ensure that reminders are scheduled correctly even when the device's wall-clock time is adjusted due to Daylight Saving Time (DST).\n\n**Native Test Gate:**\n- **Unit Tests:** Ensure that all functions in `reminder-alert-plan.ts` and `reminder-alerts.native.ts` are covered by unit tests.\n- **Integration Tests:** Test the interaction between the front-end and back-end to ensure that reminders are scheduled and canceled correctly.\n- **End-to-End (E2E) Tests:** Simulate user interactions to ensure that the lock-screen reminder privacy and six-occurrence scheduling horizon work as expected.\n\n### Evidence-Based Options with Product Recommendation, Drawbacks, and Benign Acceptance Checks\n\n#### Lock-Screen Reminder Privacy\n\n**Product Recommendation:**\n- **Feature:** Allow users to opt-in or opt-out of lock-screen reminders per reminder.\n- **Implementation:** Add a boolean field `showOnLockScreen` to the `ReminderForAlert` type and modify the notification scheduling logic to respect this field.\n\n**Drawbacks:**\n- **Complexity:** Adding per-reminder settings increases complexity.\n- **User Experience:** Users may find it confusing to manage settings for each reminder.\n\n**Benign Acceptance Checks:**\n- **Unit Tests:** Ensure that the notification scheduling logic correctly respects the `showOnLockScreen` field.\n- **Integration Tests:** Test that reminders are scheduled and canceled correctly when the `showOnLockScreen` field is toggled.\n\n#### Six-Occurrence Scheduling Horizon\n\n**Product Recommendation:**\n- **Feature:** Allow reminders to be scheduled up to six occurrences in the future.\n- **Implementation:** Modify the `planReminderAlerts` function to allow up to six occurrences.\n\n**Drawbacks:**\n- **Complexity:** Adding a configurable scheduling horizon increases complexity.\n- **User Experience:** Users may find it confusing to manage reminders for multiple occurrences.\n\n**Benign Acceptance Checks:**\n- **Unit Tests:** Ensure that the `planReminderAlerts` function correctly schedules up to six occurrences.\n- **Integration Tests:** Test that reminders are scheduled and canceled correctly when the scheduling horizon is set to six occurrences.\n\n#### Local Wall-Clock Recurrence and DST Handling\n\n**Product Recommendation:**\n- **Feature:** Ensure that reminders are scheduled correctly even when the device's wall-clock time is adjusted due to DST.\n- **Implementation:** Modify the `localDate` function to handle DST correctly.\n\n**Drawbacks:**\n- **Complexity:** Handling DST correctly increases complexity.\n- **User Experience:** Users may not notice the difference, but it is important for accurate scheduling.\n\n**Benign Acceptance Checks:**\n- **Unit Tests:** Ensure that the `localDate` function correctly handles DST.\n- **Integration Tests:** Test that reminders are scheduled and canceled correctly when the device's wall-clock time is adjusted due to DST.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe proposed changes are necessary to improve the user experience and ensure accurate scheduling of reminders. The product decision and native test gate are well-defined, and the evidence-based options with product recommendation, drawbacks, and benign acceptance checks provide a clear path forward.",
